-- title:
--   Central–elliptic comparison for cyclic base change, constant displayed
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension whose degree $[L:K]$ is prime (`hprime`). Let $0 < \alpha < \beta$ be real numbers. On the $L$-side, $\Phi_L$ is a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ contained in the determinant slab $\{g \mid \mathrm{ideleNorm}_L(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΦs`), where [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19) is the real value of the module character `distribHaarChar` of the adele ring at an idele, and $\Phi_L$ is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) (the map induced by $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$) acting on the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` restricted to that slab (`hΦ`). Further, $\nu_{Z L}$ is a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\Omega_L$ a fundamental domain for the subgroup of principal ideles, the image of $L^\times$, with respect to $\nu_{ZL}$ (`hΩL`). The datum $D$ is an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is continuous in each component and compatible with $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$. The automorphism $\sigma$ is a nontrivial element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ ($h\sigma$) such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`hgen`). The finite set $S_K$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$ is such that every prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ whose restriction to $\mathcal{O}_K$ lies outside $S_K$ has ramification index $1$ (`hS`).
--
--   Characters. The homomorphism $\xi_L$ from the top subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ has continuous associated $\mathbb{C}$-valued function (`hξc`) and is trivial on the principal ideles (`hξt`). The finite set $\Xi$ of homomorphisms from the top subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ consists, by `hΞ`, exactly of those $\xi$ that are continuous, trivial on the principal ideles of $K$, and satisfy $\xi \circ \mathcal{N} = \xi_L$, where $\mathcal{N}$ is the idelic norm `idelicNorm` of the base change [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87), that is `Units.map` of the algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_L \to \mathbb{A}_K$ taken along $\beta$.
--
--   Levels, types and the $K$-side geometry. $N$ is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ and $\mathrm{tys}_L$ an [`AutomorphicForm.ArchTypeFamily L`](def/AutomorphicForm_IsotypicCuspSpace.html#L728) (a finite family of archimedean representation types at each infinite place); $N'$ is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and $\mathrm{tys}_K$ an `ArchTypeFamily K`. The set $\Phi_K \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ lies in the slab $\{g \mid \mathrm{ideleNorm}_K(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΦKs`) and is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ with respect to `adelicGLHaar` restricted to that slab (`hΦK`); $\nu_{ZK}$ is a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ and $\Omega_K$ a fundamental domain for the principal ideles of $K$ (`hΩK`).
--
--   Haar factorisation constants. Positive reals $c_K, c_L$ are given together with two hypotheses. `hG` states: for every finite set $S$ of primes of $K$, every $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, every $f_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles and every family $f_S$ of functions on the local groups $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, if $f_a$ and the $f_S(v)$ for $v \in S$ are almost everywhere strongly measurable for `archHaarK` and `localHaar`, if $f(g) = f_a(g_\infty)\prod_{v \in S} f_S(v)(g_v)$ whenever all components of $g$ outside $S$ lie in `localIntegralSet`, and if $f(g) = 0$ whenever some component outside $S$ fails to lie there, then $\int f \, d(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}) = c_K \cdot (\int f_a \, d\,\mathrm{archHaarK}) \cdot \prod_{v \in S} \int f_S(v) \, d\,\mathrm{localHaar}$. The hypothesis `hG'` is the semi-local counterpart over $L$: the same shape of factorisation, with constant $c_L$, for the pushforward of `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ along the inverse of the isomorphism obtained from `Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57), the factors being `archHaarL` and the semi-local Haar measures `semiLocalHaar`, and the integrality conditions being membership of `tensorPlace` images in `semiLocalIntegralSet`.
--
--   The subgroups $A_K$ and $N^1$. The subgroup $A_K \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is closed (`hAKc`) and consists exactly of the images of ideles of $K$ under `Units.map` of the ring map $\beta$ of the genuine base change (`hAK`); $\mu_{A_K}$ is a Haar measure on $A_K$ whose integrals against $\nu_{ZK}$ agree under this identification, i.e. $\int_{A_K} g \, d\mu_{A_K} = \int_{\mathbb{A}_K^\times} g(\beta_*(a)) \, d\nu_{ZK}$ for all $g$ (`hμAK`). The subgroup $N^1 \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is closed (`hN1c`) and consists exactly of the ideles of idelic norm $1$ (`hN1`); $\mu_N$ is a Haar measure on $N^1$ and $c_N > 0$ a constant such that for every $g : \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ one has $\int_{N^1} g \, d\mu_N = c_N \int_{\mathbb{A}_L^\times/A_K} g\big(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}(\sigma^{-1})(q.\mathrm{out}) \cdot q.\mathrm{out}^{-1}\big) \, d(\mathrm{HaarQuotient.measure}\ \nu_{ZL}\,A_K\,\mu_{A_K})$, the quotient being the orbit space of the $A_K$-action and the quotient measure the pushforward of $\nu_{ZL}$ weighted by [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25) (`hNc`).
--
--   The norm-fibre constant. A positive real $C$ is given with two hypotheses. `hCl`: for every measurable $g$ with values in $[0,\infty]$, the lower integral over the orbit space $\mathbb{A}_L^\times/N^1$ of $g(\mathcal{N}(q.\mathrm{out}))$ against [`HaarQuotient.measure`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28) $\nu_{ZL}\,N^1\,\mu_N$ equals $\mathrm{ofReal}(C)$ times the lower integral of $g$ over the range of $\mathcal{N}$ against $\nu_{ZK}$. `hCi`: for every measurable $g : \mathbb{A}_K^\times \to \mathbb{C}$, the function $q \mapsto g(\mathcal{N}(q.\mathrm{out}))$ is integrable for that quotient measure if and only if $g$ is integrable on the range of $\mathcal{N}$ for $\nu_{ZK}$, and the corresponding Bochner integrals satisfy the same identity with factor $C$.
--
--   Assertion. Under these hypotheses, for every finite set $S'$ of primes of $K$ with $S_K \subseteq S'$, and for all test functions subject to the following conditions — $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ continuous with compact support and `IsUnitFactorizableAboveOfType K L tysL` at level `levelOne (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L` over $S'$ (bi-invariance under that subgroup, the existence of a semi-local factorisation into archimedean, finite and semi-local test factors above $S'$, and archimedean bi-finiteness for $\mathrm{tys}_L$), where `finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L` is the kernel of `glArch`; $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$ continuous with compact support and `IsUnitFactorizableOfTypeAt K tysK` at level `principalLevel (𝓞 K) K N' ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K` over $S'$ (bi-invariance, a factorisation into archimedean, finite and local test factors, and archimedean bi-finiteness for $\mathrm{tys}_K$); the matching condition [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingAt K L σ.symm S' φ f`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L557), asserting the existence of factorisations of $\varphi$ and $f$ whose archimedean factors match in the twisted orbital-integral sense for $\sigma^{-1}$ and whose factors at each $v \in S'$ match locally; and the hypothesis `_hunit`, requiring for every $v \notin S'$ all of whose primes of $L$ above it are unramified that the indicator functions of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` and of `localIntegralSet K v` are matching local data for $\sigma^{-1}$ — the following identity of complex numbers holds.
--
--   The left-hand side is
--   $$\int_{\Phi_L} \int_{\Omega_L} \xi_L(z) \sum_{\delta}^{f} \varphi\big(x^{-1} \cdot \delta \cdot \sigma^{-1}_{\mathbb{A}}(z x)\big)\, d\nu_{ZL}(z)\, d(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar})(x),$$
--   where $\delta$ runs (as a finite-support sum `∑ᶠ`) over the set of $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ for which there exists $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ lying in `ellipticCell K` (the characteristic polynomial of $\gamma$ has no root in $K$) or in `centralCell K` (the matrix of $\gamma$ is a scalar multiple of the identity) with [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta$ equal to the conjugacy class of $\gamma$; here $\delta$ is taken in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ through `globalPoints`, $z$ through the central scalar embedding `centralScalar`, and $\sigma^{-1}_{\mathbb{A}}$ denotes [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14), the entrywise action of $D.\mathrm{act}(\sigma^{-1})$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$.
--
--   The right-hand side is the real constant
--   $$\frac{c_L}{c_K} \cdot c_N \cdot C \cdot \frac{\nu_{ZL}\big(\Omega_L \cap \{z \mid \mathrm{ideleNorm}_L(z) \in [1,e]\}\big)}{\nu_{ZK}\big(\Omega_K \cap \{a \mid \mathrm{ideleNorm}_K(a) \in [1,e]\}\big)} \cdot \frac{1}{\max(1, |\Xi|)},$$
--   with the two measures taken as real numbers via `toReal`, viewed as a complex number and multiplied by
--   $$\sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{\Phi_K} \int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\Big( \mathrm{adelicKernelCentralPart}_K(f)(x, zx) + \mathrm{adelicKernelEllipticPart}_K(f)(x, zx) \Big) d\nu_{ZK}(z)\, d(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar})(x),$$
--   where $zx$ abbreviates `centralScalar (𝓞 K) K z * x`, and where `adelicKernelCentralPart K f x y` is the finite-support sum $\sum_{\gamma \in \mathrm{centralCell}\,K}^{f} f(x^{-1} \gamma y)$ and `adelicKernelEllipticPart K f x y` the corresponding sum over `ellipticCell K`, the elements $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ being mapped into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ by `globalPoints`.
--
--   This is the central–elliptic row of the comparison of trace formulae underlying cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ in prime degree: the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted fold over the classes of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose twisted norm class is central or elliptic over $K$ is identified with the sum, over the idele class characters of $K$ base-changing to $\xi_L$, of the central plus elliptic part of the adelic kernel for $f$, the proportionality constant being given here in closed form in terms of the Haar factorisation constants $c_L/c_K$, the Hilbert-90 transport constant $c_N$, the norm-fibre constant $C$, the volumes of the two idele class fundamental domains in the slab $[1,e]$, and $\max(1,|\Xi|)$. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.centralEllipticConstant_eq_of_factorization_of_normFibre_of_exists_ne_zero`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.centralEllipticConstant_eq_of_factorization_of_normFibre_of_exists_ne_zero) to pin down the comparison constant once one of the two sides is known to be nonzero.
